From dc0a8b155540f2a37a9b188999a6b88123a3b2eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Alonso <nick@drkm.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:26:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Inkling: keep the shared experts folded into the routed
 gather

Measured back to back in one GPU hold on the 2-bit checkpoint (bench/K2
hold 3, p_short and p_8k, 3 runs each), the dense shared-expert layout of
the previous commit was 7-13% slower at both prefill and decode than one
gather_qmm chain over the 258 experts, so the fold stays. The docstring and
the tests added since are kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mlx_lm/models/inkling_mm_model.py | 77 ++++++++++++-------------------
 tests/test_inkling.py             | 76 +++++++++++++-----------------
 2 files changed, 62 insertions(+), 91 deletions(-)

